[2026-01-31T16:38:47.252080] I have analyzed the sequential BFS algorithm and chosen the level-synchronous parallelization strategy. This approach processes the graph level by level, parallelizing the discovery of neighbors for all nodes in the current frontier. To ensure the output is identical to the sequential version for differential testing, I will sort the collected neighbors at the end of each level before they form the next frontier. This guarantees determinism. Rejected alternatives include parallelizing the inner neighbor loop (too fine-grained), task-based work-stealing (non-deterministic), and graph partitioning (too complex for this context). My next step is to set up the baseline files.
